Based on my analysis of the codebase, I understand that I need to implement a function that calculates the diagonal elements for the mode annihilation operator. From the physics context, the diagonal elements of the annihilation operator a are √(n+1) for n=0 to cutoff-2.

```cpp
std::vector<dcomp> calculate_mode_annihilation_diagonal(size_t cutoff) {
    if (cutoff <= 1) return std::vector<dcomp>(0);

    std::vector<dcomp> result(cutoff - 1);
    for (size_t n = 0; n < cutoff - 1; ++n) {
        result[n] = std::sqrt(static_cast<double>(n + 1));
    }
    return result;
}
